From: Project Luma <noreply@projectluma.org>
Subject: [PATCH] audio-capture: add the Audio Capture portal

org.freedesktop.portal.AudioCapture lets an application record the sound
other applications play after the user chose which: one or more
applications, or all sound except the caller's own. It follows the
ScreenCast portal: CreateSession, SelectSources (types, multiple,
audio_mode with the ScreenCast v7 values, restore_token, persist_mode),
Start and OpenPipeWireRemote, with restore tokens kept by the frontend
in the "audio-capture" permission table.

The backend (org.freedesktop.impl.portal.AudioCapture) shows the choice
and returns exactly one PipeWire node carrying the chosen sound. The
remote handed to the application sees that node only: core rwx, node
factory r, the node rx, everything else hidden, with the same client
properties as a ScreenCast remote.

Tests: tests/test_audiocapture.py with a dbusmock backend template.
---
